# C++ Coding Standards

## Language Standard

- **Target**: C++20 (ISO/IEC 14882:2020)
- **Minimum**: C++17 compatible
- **Migration**: Gradual adoption of modern features

## Modern C++ Features to Use

### Smart Pointers
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Use smart pointers
std::unique_ptr<CConnection> m_pConnection;
std::shared_ptr<CResource> m_pSharedResource;

// ❌ Bad: Raw pointers for ownership
CConnection* m_pConnection;  // Avoid unless necessary
```

### Auto Type Deduction
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Use auto when type is obvious
auto strFileName = _T("file.txt");
for (const auto& file : files) { ... }

// ✅ Good: Use auto for iterators and complex types
auto it = std::find_if(files.begin(), files.end(),
    [](const CFile& f) { return f.GetSize() > 1000000; });

// ❌ Bad: Verbose types when auto is clearer
CString strFileName = _T("file.txt");

// ⚠️ Note: In MFC code, sometimes explicit types are preferred for clarity
// especially when working with MFC types like CString, CList, etc.
```

### Range-Based For Loops
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Range-based for
for (const auto& file : files) {
    ProcessFile(file);
}

// ❌ Bad: Manual iteration
for (size_t i = 0; i < files.size(); i++) {
    ProcessFile(files[i]);
}
```

### nullptr
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Use nullptr
CConnection* pConn = nullptr;
if (pConn != nullptr) { ... }

// ❌ Bad: Use NULL
CConnection* pConn = NULL;
```

### constexpr
```cpp
// ✅ Good: constexpr for compile-time constants
constexpr size_t MAX_BUFFER_SIZE = 8192;
constexpr size_t KILOBYTE = 1024;

// ❌ Bad: #define macros
#define MAX_BUFFER_SIZE 8192
```

### override and final
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Use override keyword
class CDownload : public CTransfer {
public:
    void OnComplete() override { ... }
    void OnError() override final { ... }
};

// ❌ Bad: Missing override
void OnComplete() { ... }  // Compiler won't catch mistakes
```

### Optional Values
```cpp
// ✅ Good: std::optional for optional values
std::optional<CString> FindUserName(DWORD nUserID);

// ❌ Bad: Empty string as "not found"
CString FindUserName(DWORD nUserID);  // Returns empty if not found
```

### Structured Bindings
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Structured bindings
auto [success, value] = GetStatus();
for (const auto& [key, value] : map) { ... }

// ❌ Bad: Manual unpacking
std::pair<bool, int> result = GetStatus();
bool success = result.first;
```

## Memory Management

### RAII Principles
```cpp
// ✅ Good: RAII with smart pointers
void ProcessFile(const CString& strPath) {
    auto pFile = std::make_unique<CFile>();
    if (!pFile->Open(strPath)) {
        throw std::runtime_error("Failed to open file");
    }
    // Automatic cleanup
}

// ❌ Bad: Manual cleanup
void ProcessFileBad(const CString& strPath) {
    CFile* pFile = new CFile();
    if (!pFile->Open(strPath)) {
        delete pFile;  // Easy to forget
        return;
    }
    delete pFile;  // Must remember
}
```

### Reserve Capacity
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Reserve capacity when size is known
std::vector<CString> files;
files.reserve(expectedCount);

// ❌ Bad: Multiple reallocations
std::vector<CString> files;  // Will reallocate multiple times
```

## Code Organization

### Header Files
```cpp
#pragma once

// System includes (alphabetical)
#include <memory>
#include <string>
#include <vector>

// MFC includes
#include <afx.h>
#include <afxwin.h>

// Project includes
#include "DownloadTypes.h"
#include "HashFunction.h"

// Forward declarations
class CConnection;
class CDownloadSource;

// Class definition
class CDownloadTask {
    // ...
};
```

### Implementation Files
```cpp
#include "stdafx.h"
#include "DownloadTask.h"
#include "Connection.h"

// Static member initialization
const int CDownloadTask::DEFAULT_TIMEOUT = 30000;

// Constructor with member initialization
CDownloadTask::CDownloadTask()
    : m_state(DownloadState::Idle)
    , m_priority(Priority::Normal)
{
}
```

## MFC-Specific Considerations

### BOOL vs bool
```cpp
// ✅ Good: Use BOOL for MFC member variables and API compatibility
class CConnection {
    BOOL m_bConnected;      // MFC convention
    BOOL m_bInitiated;      // MFC convention
};

// ✅ Good: Use bool for local variables and modern C++ code
bool bExists = FileExists(strPath);
if (bExists) { ... }

// ⚠️ Note: MFC uses BOOL (int) for compatibility with Windows APIs
```

### Exception Specifications
```cpp
// ⚠️ Legacy: throw() is deprecated but still used in codebase
inline CLockedBuffer GetInput() const throw() { ... }

// ✅ Modern: Use noexcept instead
inline CLockedBuffer GetInput() const noexcept { ... }

// Note: When updating legacy code, prefer noexcept over throw()
```

## Avoid

- Raw pointers for ownership (use smart pointers)
- NULL instead of nullptr (prefer nullptr, but NULL exists in legacy code)
- #define for constants (use constexpr)
- Manual memory management when RAII is possible
- Missing override keyword on virtual functions
- Unnecessary copies (use references)
- Mixing BOOL and bool inconsistently (use BOOL for MFC members, bool for locals)
